NAME
       dirname - print the directory part of a path

SYNOPSIS
       dirname PATH...

DESCRIPTION
       dirname removes the last slash and everything after it from each PATH
       and prints the rest. A name without a slash gives ".". Like basename,
       it works on the text only.

EXAMPLES
           dirname /etc/sysconfig/network      prints /etc/sysconfig
           dirname report.txt                  prints .

       In a script, find the directory the script itself is in:

           here=$(dirname "$0")

SEE ALSO
       basename(1), realpath(1)
